description:
simulation/src/economy/market.rs:1125 contains a live dbg! macro in shipped code:

    let price_workers = recipe.duration.minutes()
        * company.n_workers as f64
        * WORKER_CONSUMPTION_PER_MINUTE;

    dbg!(price_consumption, price_workers, qty);

    let newprice = (price_consumption
        + Money::new_inner((price_workers.inner() as f32 * price_multiplier) as i64))
        / qty;

This is on MAIN, not on a branch. dbg! writes to stderr unconditionally in both debug and release builds - it is not compiled out like debug_assert.

MEASURED IMPACT: found by wiring-auditor 2026-08-27 while running the 250k benchmark contract at reduced scale. It printed 23 lines of 'price_workers = 1.66$' into stderr BEFORE any benchmark result appeared, polluting the output of the very command the benchmark exists to make trustworthy. At real scale the volume scales with the number of companies times price updates per tick.

WHY IT MATTERS BEYOND NOISE: it is unbounded I/O on a per-tick hot path. stderr writes are synchronous and can block. This is a plausible contributor to per-tick cost in any profiling run, which makes every benchmark number taken so far suspect until it is removed.

TRAP: check git log -S 'dbg!' before deleting - if it was left deliberately for an open investigation, the owner should be asked first. Also sweep for other live dbg! occurrences rather than fixing only this one.

native_app/src/gui/hud/time_controls.rs, the time_button closure at lines 64-82.

  if b.show().clicked {
      if b_warp == 0 {
          if *warp == 0 {
              *warp = *depause_warp;   // line 75
          } else {
              *depause_warp = *warp;
          }
      }
      *warp = b_warp;                  // line 80
  }

Line 80 is OUTSIDE the b_warp == 0 branch, so it runs on every click. When the player clicks the pause button while the game is ALREADY paused (b_warp == 0 and *warp == 0), line 75 restores the saved speed and line 80 immediately overwrites it with 0. The game stays paused. Clicking pause a second time does nothing.

The other click path is fine: when running (*warp != 0), line 77 saves depause_warp and line 80 pauses correctly.

WHY IT SURVIVED: the keyboard path at lines 30-35 is a correct toggle and is unaffected. Anyone testing with the PausePlay hotkey sees working behaviour. Only the on-screen button is broken.

FOUND BY: rustc warning 'value assigned to *warp is never read' (unused_assignments) at line 75, surfaced in editor diagnostics 2026-08-27. The dead store IS the bug, not a style nit.

TRAP: do not silence the warning. Also do not simply move line 80 into an else branch without checking the b_warp != 0 buttons still set speed on click - that path currently depends on line 80 running unconditionally.

LANE: native_app/ is ui-implementer. Per the project delivery rule, UI behaviour is proven by an eyeballed frame, not by a sim test - the sim harness cannot drive the UI.
